<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>German power grid sabotage attack linked to ‘climate extremism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:694da36134db6b1893df99034dcee01c332669bbc96630c858ae40db1bbabed8</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:40:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-german-power-grid-sabotage-attack-linked-to-climate-extremism--b5a9f0391572.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-german-power-grid-sabotage-attack-linked-to-climate-extremism" /><summary type="html">German Interior Minister Alexander Dobrindt on Friday said the evidence in a recent spate of sabotage attacks on power grids across the country points to a militant climate activist.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s ‘Most Dangerous Man’: PR gift for the AfD?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3c74bd712e4eaf51604d024777b88e83df5ab6d49ec4095d3883b8b18725dff</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:31:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260904-germany-s-most-dangerous-man-pr-gift-for-the-afd--f852f5df9336.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260904-germany-s-most-dangerous-man-pr-gift-for-the-afd" /><summary type="html">The Ukrainian capital was hit by Russia’s most intense wave of air attacks on Kyiv, reportedly in four years, with Reuters describing air raid sirens, drones, cruise and ballistic missiles exhausting Ukraine’s defence system, with 12 people killed and the Ukrainian foreign minister making a direct appeal to Western allies for more Patriot interceptor missiles.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>'Italian opposition fragmented: No alternative leader, no other possible leader than Giorgia Meloni'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f52e920a61688b156df64f7d2b9ba87c64e65f87108272a873450f9008978ce</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:35:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italian-opposition-fragmented-no-alternative-leader-no-other-possible-leader-than-giorgia-m--1c36e6864261.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italian-opposition-fragmented-no-alternative-leader-no-other-possible-leader-than-giorgia-meloni-1" /><summary type="html">Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Political analyst Lorenzo Pregliasco, co-founder of polling agency YouTrend and adjunct professor at the University of Bologna. He argues that Giorgia Meloni’s unusual longevity in office is best understood not simply as a record of political strength, but as the product of a carefully calibrated governing strategy. Meloni has maintained stability partly by avoiding structural reforms disruptive enough to mobilize multiple constituencies against her at once. Her dominance within Fratelli d’Italia, the absence of a credible alternative leader, and a fragmented opposition have reinforced that advantage.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider, the ideologist behind the AFD’s plans in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5563bd0ce66277997a997d82fe5a4b99581970c5968a014541e30aa42e4c28f</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:34:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-germany-hans-thomas-tillschneider-the-ideologist-behind-the-afd-s-plans-in-saxony-anhalt--220beb71b19c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-germany-hans-thomas-tillschneider-the-ideologist-behind-the-afd-s-plans-in-saxony-anhalt" /><summary type="html">The far-right German political party Alternative for Germany could win a historical victory in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt in key elections this Sunday. The party’s agenda is more radical than ever and inspired by the proposals of an influential ideologist in the region: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France announces €1 billion aid for farmers after climate-hit summer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5aae5509176d003486243db340befada2c14262457cd0701a370c2a545dfb98c</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:12:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-france-announces-_1-billion-aid-for-farmers-after-climate-hit-summer--e6ed56d5d705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-france-announces-%E2%82%AC1-billion-aid-for-farmers-after-climate-hit-summer" /><summary type="html">France has recorded its hottest summer on record this year as the country battled heatwaves, drought and massive wildfires. The extreme weather has continued into September, with France's national weather service placing five departments on orange alert for several days. Temperatures are expected to reach 40°C in some areas. France's agriculture minister also announced a plan to unlock over 1 billion euros in aid to the agriculture sector, which has been severely affected by the extreme weather.</summary></entry><entry><title>Strengthening Africa is an investment in Europe's future: EU Commissioner Jozef Sikela</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32194e8b0120cca153d1a8bd90cee31590b6b91472914200eecffa17fb8c08d7</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:03:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-strengthening-africa-is-an-investment-in-europe-s-future-eu-commissioner-jozef-sikela--f05b28eefbd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-strengthening-africa-is-an-investment-in-europe-s-future-eu-commissioner-jozef-sikela" /><summary type="html">Are great-power politics back, at the expense of smaller countries? In an age of strongmen, is multilateralism in retreat? Not according to Jozef Sikela. The EU Commissioner in charge of International Partnerships insists that traditional multilateralism is alive and well, especially in the EU's approach to Africa and to the Arctic. We sat down with him for an interview at the European Commission in Brussels.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian drone strikes Ukraine security service HQ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d65280cab02168df0a81890b5541fdfeebf966aa622658c9ec1b0138413d8dd6</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:59:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-russian-drone-aimed-directly-at-ukraine-security-service-hq-zelensky-says--9847636126d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-russian-drone-aimed-directly-at-ukraine-security-service-hq-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">A Russian drone struck the headquarters of Ukraine's SBU security services in Kyiv on Friday afternoon, said Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, injuring five people. The attack followed a series of deadly overnight strikes across Ukraine, including the southern Odesa region.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Meloni celebrates milestone as Italy's longest-lasting government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fe7c7e1d9b0c960cc55550cfe35b9382bfe2c60df064459b3f1b5e87de00670</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:50:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-meloni-celebrates-milestone-as-italy-s-longest-lasting-government--f397a1fc9a52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-meloni-celebrates-milestone-as-italy-s-longest-lasting-government" /><summary type="html">Italy's Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni is celebrating a milestone: her hard-right government is now the longest-lasting in the country's post war history. In a country known for its political instability, it's a notable record. But considerable challenges remain for Italy's first female prime minister, ahead of elections next year. FRANCE 24's Italy correspondent Seema Gupta reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Struggling to make its voice heard: Can the EU forge a true foreign policy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:415164a10f4996f1b126220b8e60152ec1cc9074747d7043c87a95b1f360d11e</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:42:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-struggling-to-make-its-voice-heard-can-the-eu-forge-a-true-foreign-policy--d3fdfae86cb4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-struggling-to-make-its-voice-heard-can-the-eu-forge-a-true-foreign-policy" /><summary type="html">"Who do I call if I want to speak to Europe?" The famous quote attributed to Henry Kissinger still resonates today. There is in fact a Mrs Europe on the world stage: Kaja Kallas, the EU High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy. She is actually the sixth high representative. But ever since that post was created, rivalries between different centres of power have diluted the EU's ability to speak with one voice. We saw that recently with tensions over who should represent the EU in any potential talks with Russia.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Strength of Meloni less linked to policy, more about her party's dominance within govt coalition</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fd951450b5e347130668aa335468ceb6a45040063ad162cf910a0d16b80ac12</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:24:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/strength-of-meloni-less-linked-to-policy-more-about-her-party-s-dominance-within-govt-coalition--987072e3c262.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/strength-of-meloni-less-linked-to-policy-more-about-her-party-s-dominance-within-govt-coalition" /><summary type="html">William Hilderbrandt is pleased to welcome Dr. Giulia Sandri, Associate researcher at the Free University of Brussels. Meloni has benefited from something historically scarce in Italian politics: longevity. Four years of governmental stability have allowed her to accumulate diplomatic relationships, strengthening Italy’s position within Europe and giving Rome greater visibility internationally. Yet Sandri argues that this political success sits alongside a much less decisive domestic record. Improvements in employment and fiscal credibility coexist with weak growth, stagnant wages, declining purchasing power and persistent structural problems in healthcare, education, demographics and public administration.</summary></entry><entry><title>What does acquittal in the Daphne Caruana Galizia case mean for journalists?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ca1a3a71e050b8b501a44f61bfb37a5ca4f028e72b16ad8a2cbe40689cea1f4</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:07:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20260904-what-does-acquittal-in-the-daphne-caruana-galizia-case-mean-for-journalists--f23eee59cc84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20260904-what-does-acquittal-in-the-daphne-caruana-galizia-case-mean-for-journalists" /><summary type="html">This week, FRANCE 24's media show Scoop looks at the murder of anti-corruption journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. Press freedom groups are furious after Maltese businessman Yorgen Fenech was acquitted of involvement. Caruana Galizia was an outspoken critic of the government and described as a "one-woman WikiLeaks". She was killed by a car bomb in 2017 and speculation followed that influential figures may have been involved. Our guest is the Times of Malta Editor-in-Chief, Herman Grech.</summary><category term="Scoop" /></entry><entry><title>Stability or fiasco? Giorgia Meloni becomes longest-serving Italian PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2d844cf98096685c65763ab74e682618bd8251bd9acd76776e7337d95241081</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260904-stability-or-fiasco-giorgia-meloni-becomes-longest-serving-italian-pm--c8766e845af9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260904-stability-or-fiasco-giorgia-meloni-becomes-longest-serving-italian-pm" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Friday, September 4: Italy's Giorgia Meloni becomes the longest-serving prime minister in Italy's postwar history. While she's celebrated by the rightwing press, the leftwing press say her leadership is a fiasco. Also, is Europe gearing up for a chaotic winter? Concern is mounting after the UN warned of a "supersized" El Niño phenomenon that could bring heavy rains and snow. Plus we look at tributes to Gloria Steinem, journalist and women's rights icon, who has died at 92.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>German far right's breakout moment? AfD party eyes outright win in regional election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b44aa114822cc8b1aeeeac63b1865f8c4e141d9063b625eece24104caee08b6</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:29:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260904-german-far-right-s-breakout-moment-afd-party-eyes-outright-win-in-regional-election--ad40d2f059ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260904-german-far-right-s-breakout-moment-afd-party-eyes-outright-win-in-regional-election" /><summary type="html">Could Europeans awaken next Monday to another shock bellwether moment? German voters could for the first time since World War II give an outright majority to a far-right party in regional elections. We ask about the AfD's push in Saxony-Anhalt and a charismatic lead candidate whose campaign strives to put charm above the vitriol usually associated with a party with pro-Nazi roots.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Power party: Italy’s Meloni marks record as PM with major festivities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63d45e433afe422ef94fad2227c8819aea2b4dedc252f21b7c9899507e1ff959</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:31:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-italy-s-meloni-throws-party-to-celebrate-record-in-power--e7a5742401e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-italy-s-meloni-throws-party-to-celebrate-record-in-power" /><summary type="html">Georgia Meloni's Brothers of Italy (FdI) party threw a major party Friday to mark her record as the longest-serving prime minister in Italy's post-war history. Meloni has been PM for 1,413 days, beating billionaire media tycoon Silvio Berlusconi's record.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Pragmatic international relations': Sánchez seeks to avoid 'further conflict with Rabat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a528439bea6c0a1bf2c3627033e28c65007e28f432156f85f6768f6f49ea075e</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T05:22:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-pragmatic-international-relations-s_nchez-seeks-to-avoid-further-conflict-with-rabat--c4a5b9cb15c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-pragmatic-international-relations-s%C3%A1nchez-seeks-to-avoid-further-conflict-with-rabat" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Alana Moceri, International Relations Professor at IE School of Politics, Economics and Global Affairs. The migrant crossings at Ceuta have become both a domestic and international political lightning rod. At home, Pedro Sánchez faces opponents who can cast migration in existential terms, with Spain's far right amplifying the rhetoric of "invasion." Internationally, the crisis exposes the geopolitical leverage inherent in control of the border. Ceuta thus emerges as more than a migration crisis: the border becomes at once an instrument of geopolitical leverage, a weapon in Spain's domestic political contest, and a battleground for competing narratives and disinformation.</summary></entry><entry><title>'50% savvy political tactics, 50% extraordinarily good luck': The formula to Meloni's success?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d86cbba3ccf4c331e724e8899a2df3fa11efd647dd4537397d4803a40487455e</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T20:57:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260903-50-savvy-political-tactics-50-extraordinarily-good-luck-the-formula-to-meloni-s-success--93152379c303.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260903-50-savvy-political-tactics-50-extraordinarily-good-luck-the-formula-to-meloni-s-success" /><summary type="html">Giorgia Meloni's hard-right government on Friday becomes the longest lasting in Italy's postwar history – a notable record that belies considerable challenges ahead of elections next year. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Nathalie Tocci, Director of the Istituto Affari Internazionali in Rome and Professor of Practice at the John Hopkins University SAIS. She says that Meloni's success comes down to "50 percent savvy political tactics and 50 percent extraordinarily good luck".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Why Ukraine’s drained Kakhovka Dam is strategic for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8e04596d0c523d93d7430259a1904d078a240e95ca6f8ab9552a12988ef3102</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:34:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-why-ukraine-drained-kakhovka-dam-strategic-russia--143f379d846d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-why-ukraine-drained-kakhovka-dam-strategic-russia" /><summary type="html">Small groups of Russian soldiers have been inching forward through the vast, drained Kakhovka reservoir since they blew up the dam in June 2023. Russian forces are infiltrating this “no man’s land” for reconnaissance purposes rather than for a future military offensive, said a military expert.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Giorgia Meloni government becomes Italy's longest-lasting since World War II</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fd3919c2b7e990860376a7c684b7af4884685a1a530e1ad48ce8a16d1f3ae26</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:29:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-giorgia-meloni-government-becomes-italy-s-longest-lasting-since-world-war-ii--f321ed0a24d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-giorgia-meloni-government-becomes-italy-s-longest-lasting-since-world-war-ii" /><summary type="html">Italy's first female Prime Minister, Giorgia Meloni, has surpassed a longevity record set by the late Silvio Berlusconi. When she took office in 2022, many European allies viewed her with unease, given her party's neo-fascist roots. Yet she has governed pragmatically, working within EU institutions and even supporting Ukraine. Domestically, however, she has targeted same-sex parents and clamped down on press freedom.</summary></entry><entry><title>France-UK ties and humour celebrated as London receives Bayeux Tapestry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a62e14a230ae7afdc2fc45a63c3ae4a93a7b6e4d7665f480bcb6a22d3b63c638</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:27:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-uk-ties-and-humour-celebrated-as-london-receives-bayeux-tapestry-1--6ef2090555dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-uk-ties-and-humour-celebrated-as-london-receives-bayeux-tapestry-1" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel #Macron is in #London on the occasion of the #Bayeux Tapestry's exhibition at the #BritishMuseum. The 1,000-year-old work of woven art recounts the Battle of #Hastings, in which William the Conqueror – #KingCharles's ancestor – led the Norman Conquest of #England. An opportunity for the French president, the British PM Andy #Burnham and British monarch to celebrate the strong ties between the two countries.</summary></entry><entry><title>Driverless robotaxis hit the streets of London</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c68390e8de068f2e5915ebc51a17f1c544cb84346551f0aac274b3c53059e45</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:16:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-driverless-robotaxis-hit-the-streets-of-london--2660dfa1427c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-driverless-robotaxis-hit-the-streets-of-london" /><summary type="html">London is entering the era of autonomous vehicles: driverless cabs are now available through Uber and British tech firm Wayve in the capital. It marks a setback for Google's Waymo and Chinese giant Baidu, which have been eyeing Europe as a largely untapped market for autonomous vehicles. But for Wayve, it is its first mass-market rollout, and the company now plans to expand to Tokyo and 10 other cities with Uber.</summary></entry><entry><title>Murder of Daphne Caruana Galizia: Campaigner 'devastated' at tycoon's acquittal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f43d5342d6e82bea40e8d090bf16a392db3f1a0a5f57eaf8397f2431f3e3efb</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/i-m-devastated-by-the-verdict-says-tom-gibson-deputy-dir-for-committee-to-protect-journalists--f0de620fc0ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/i-m-devastated-by-the-verdict-says-tom-gibson-deputy-dir-for-committee-to-protect-journalists" /><summary type="html">A campaigner who has worked on the case of murdered Maltese journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia since she was killed by a car bomb in 2017 has spoken of his devastation at the not guilty verdict.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>France's Macron meets UK PM Burnham at Downing Street</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5b222128b0abc7352d3c3321fdc7b57930e90e59456bace734145b6ab1376d5</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T13:45:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-s-macron-meets-uk-pm-burnham-at-downing-street--e3b95d5ceaa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-s-macron-meets-uk-pm-burnham-at-downing-street" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron met Britain’s new Prime Minister, Andy Burnham, for official talks at 10 Downing Street. The meeting came a day after the pair were joined by King Charles and Queen Camilla at the British Museum for a preview of the Bayeux Tapestry exhibition in London. Macron is the first EU leader to meet Burnham. Talks are expected to cover relations between Britain and the European Union, support for Ukraine, and migrant crossings in the English Channel.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's Sanchez says no 'solid proof' that Morocco planned Ceuta crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd5822318cffa42dcd37b048923961e42b9504cf98ef1323ee4a489908ce72fe</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T11:58:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-spain-s-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-that-morocco-planned-ceuta-crisis--4482acec72d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-spain-s-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-that-morocco-planned-ceuta-crisis" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez has told lawmakers that there is no evidence the Ceuta migrant crisis was orchestrated by Morocco's government. His remarks come a day after tens of thousands of people took part in protests across the country to criticize his handling of the migrant influx. He acknowledged that Ceuta was both a humanitarian crisis and an administrative challenge. But he rejected the findings of a police report that seemed to lay blame on Morocco. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin's 'global battle' against US, NATO: Russia 'testing' NATO since 2022 Ukraine invasion began</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3050a0ee47e08d6ef46195f5a5c3fd52460865b5c410bb6344521e419047de36</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:26:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260903-putin-s-global-battle-against-us-nato-russia-testing-nato-since-2022-ukraine-invasion-began--62697efb03cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260903-putin-s-global-battle-against-us-nato-russia-testing-nato-since-2022-ukraine-invasion-began" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Anna Borshchevskaya, Senior Fellow at The Washington Institute. She interprets Russia's reported missile support for Iran not as an isolated arms transaction, but as part of a broader geopolitical strategy in which Moscow treats Ukraine, Iran, NATO and the United States as interconnected fronts. In her analysis, Vladimir Putin’s objective is less about pursuing direct military confrontation with Washington than about altering the strategic environment around it: strengthening actors hostile to the United States, increasing the costs of American and Israeli military action, and repeatedly probing Western thresholds for retaliation.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Meloni government sets longevity record in Italy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:573aef53bfbf463a581db149c9b97ff2c1af5e0bd5c78171db71cd78fe6e4e19</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:11:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-meloni-government-sets-longevity-record-in-italy--a69c834200f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-meloni-government-sets-longevity-record-in-italy" /><summary type="html">Giorgia Meloni's hard-right government has been in power for 1,413 days. She surpassed the record set by Silvio Berlusconi between 2001 and 2005, making her government Italy's longest serving uninterrupted government since World War II, after a period of intense instability. Italy has had 68 governments in the last 80 years. Giorgia Meloni and her party will celebrate the feat on Friday with a huge pre-election rally in the southern city of Bari. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta tells more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Norway seizes Russian ship to enforce $4.22 billion Ukrainian compensation claim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8de1cfb5bd71c7c063d6fd00501092792d97ea08423f07d806e10300d186ff3b</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:07:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-norway-seizes-russian-ship-to-enforce-4-22-billion-ukrainian-arbitration-claim--8ffd5a80a237.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-norway-seizes-russian-ship-to-enforce-4-22-billion-ukrainian-arbitration-claim" /><summary type="html">Norway said Wednesday it had seized a Russian ship as part of a Ukrainian effort to recover $4.22 billion awarded to state energy firm Naftogaz over Russia’s seizure of its assets in Crimea in 2014. The Professor Molchanov vessel was detained off the Arctic Svalbard archipelago after a Norwegian court ordered its arrest.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>No 'solid proof' Morocco planned Ceuta migrant rush, says Spanish PM Sanchez</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4506e0cfcfc145ffa203a75d0136b62ec35906e2bbf4894f550e384841fc58c</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T08:18:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-morocco-planned-ceuta-migrant-rush--1ed53eaa7182.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-morocco-planned-ceuta-migrant-rush" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said Thursday there was no "solid proof" that Morocco orchestrated a migrant rush into Ceuta in July following the emergence of a police report highlighting multiple failings by Moroccan security forces.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Churchillian moment? Macron in Britain amid scramble to boost European defence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5e78927f35dd29855c5a4ccba877cdd2212c93728fcea41a3b32114efd474ce</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T07:39:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260903-churchillian-moment-macron-in-britain-amid-scramble-to-boost-european-defence--13e2ba2d0940.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260903-churchillian-moment-macron-in-britain-amid-scramble-to-boost-european-defence" /><summary type="html">What can an 11th-century comic strip about the Norman Conquest of England tell us about the spectre of sea change in 2026 Europe? France’s president is on hand for the hottest ticket in London, the first-ever cross-Channel visit of the Bayeux Tapestry, which, for the record, is not a tapestry but a delicate scroll of embroidered cloth that chronicles a radical turning point in our continent’s history. Should France’s outgoing president and the British monarch who welcomes him be likened more to the defending Saxons or the invading Normans?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Macron, Burnham hold talks on migrants, EU after viewing Bayeux Tapestry in London</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8800662b11ba2292ed6dc5af8ffc5e805eefbefc801986d375190c321cca447</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T06:47:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-macron-to-hold-first-talks-with-uk-s-burnham-after-viewing-bayeux-tapestry-in-london--cf8928d0a830.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-macron-to-hold-first-talks-with-uk-s-burnham-after-viewing-bayeux-tapestry-in-london" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham held their first talks on Thursday after meeting a day earlier at the Bayeux Tapestry exhibition at the British Museum. Topping the agenda were several issues, including migrant boats crossing the Channel, British-EU relations and the Ukraine war.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
